# Artifact Hygiene

- Do not commit heavy temporary outputs when canonical summaries are sufficient.
- Keep canonical outputs in stable, phase-identified locations.
- Separate temporary/debug artifacts from official scientific outputs.
- If heavy artifacts are needed externally, keep references, metadata, and integrity hashes in-repo.
- Respect `.gitignore` constraints and avoid introducing noisy binary churn.

## Practical default

- Prefer reproducible scripts + canonical CSV/MD over raw bulk run dumps.
